# This file was the Dynamics 365 Business Central (AL) template chosen when the
# repository was created. There is no AL code here and never will be, so it
# ignored nothing and hid nothing — replaced with the stack this project
# actually uses: Python on the server, React on the client.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# The built SPA is produced by `npm run build` on deploy, never committed — a
# checked-in bundle drifts from its source silently.
server/spa/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local scratch
*.local

# Recorded narration.
#
# Nothing here is committed yet, so every deployment currently falls back to
# the browser's synthesiser. The `sapi` backend writes 52MB of WAV purely to
# prove the pipeline locally, and that should never be committed.
#
# WHEN REAL RECORDINGS ARE MADE (tools/build_narration.py --backend azure),
# the mp3 files, their word tracks and manifest.json ARE the deployment
# artefact and belong in the repository — about 10MB, which is the point at
# which Git LFS stops being optional. Relax this rule then.
assets/narration/
